[Normally tournament ascensions don't get posted (or it seems
so). However, since this monk is the 7th in my reverse-alphabetical
Geas, I figured I ought to post it, so's I can move on to Knights.]

adridg the non-conductive monk (not just because she's shock-resistant)
at one point decided she'd break all conducts and end up with a
two line conduct summary: species genocided and wishes used. Due
to a mistake of youthful over-enthusiasm (hey, I have a chicken,
why not get the book _now_?) she never did get around to polyselfing
into a chickatrice for stoning grenades. This made the endgame much
more, um, interesting.

[FWIW, the entire game was recorded using /dev/null's nifty tournament
software, so you can watch the whole damn thing (if you're bored) if
you like. User name adridg (I think that's the top one in the game
playback files list).]

The _reason_ adridg the non-conductive monk was going to break all
conducts was that the whole game was a series of accidents. You know,
like P becomes %, 'e'at (since monks can eat P), and then you realise
that black pudding is not vegetarian. Given the amount of food adridg
found (including a huge food store on level 3 or so) vegan conduct would
not have been difficult. But once this was broken, leprechauns were eaten,
maybe even a wraith.

A pickaxe accident led to the abandonment of weaponless conduct. Oh well.
Finding a +8 Fire Brand on Astral (in the unwilling hands of an adventurer,
but hey) was very very useful, since I hadn't considered how lousy 
martial arts are against decked-out adventurers of the riders. In retrospect,
a good distance weapon (like 20 +7 daggers) would have been most useful.
Throughout Gehennom I used a +5 silver saber, which worked reasonably
well. No amount of saccing got me any useful artifact - Orcrist and 
Trollsbane were my gifts in that department.

Some initial soul searching with an early wish led to speed boots
and not the Master Key, but I wished for an artifact later, for the
damage reduction. That really saved my ass on Astral, where I could
stand amongst a herd of 'a', 'A', and '@' and not lose appreciable
hit points - as long as no clerical spells were cast and the riders
stayed away, I was fine.

Wishes went for [SB, [HawaiianShirt, [GoDex, [HoB, a marker, and the
Master Key of Thievery. Geno'ed h and L - never had much trouble with
R, lost one point of enchantment somewhere to a disenchanter but then
realized that +MM was useful.

Did a fair amount of spellcasting in the main game, but once the amulet
started draining power, on Astral, switched to a (found) shield of
reflection and lots of amulets of life saving.

Famine and Death were not difficult to deal with. They were guarding the
wrong altars, though, and in the end I had to deal with Pestilence. I
hate having to do that, especially when all the potions I could use to
improve the experience are already gone. (Again, youthful enthusiasm,
I should have done more prepping.) That cost me my 3 amulets of
life saving (cool, there goes the "you survived" conduct). After much
trouble, killed Pestilence once and lured it around back of the
temple, so I could dash in, offer the amulet, and be done with it.

One final note, the Eyes really _do_ make Gegennom a nicer place.



